3195:
**μέλλω**, 
[in LXX: [[18-job.3.8|Job.3:8]] (עָתִיד) 19:25 (אַחֲרוֹן); elsewhere for fut., and frequently in Wi, II, 4Mac ;] 
**to be about** to be or do; 
1. with inf. (Bl., §62, 4; 68, 2; M, _Pr._, 114); 
(a) of intending or being about to do of one's own free will: with inf. praes., [[40-matthew.2.13|Mat.2:13]], [[42-luke.10.1|Luk.10:1]], [[44-acts.3.3|Act.3:3 5:35]], [[58-hebrews.8.5|Heb.8:5]], [[61-2-peter.1.12|2Pe.1:12]] (Field, _Notes_, 240), al.; with inf. aor. (Bl., §58, 3), [[44-acts.12.6|Act.12:6]], [[66-revelation.3.16|Rev.3:16]]; 
(b) **of compulsion, necessity or certainty**: with inf. praes., [[40-matthew.16.27|Mat.16:27]], [[42-luke.9.31|Luk.9:31]], [[43-john.6.71|Jhn.6:71]], [[45-romans.4.24|Rom.4:24]], al.; with inf. aor., [[45-romans.8.18|Rom.8:18]], [[48-galatians.3.23|Gal.3:23]], [[66-revelation.3.2|Rev.3:2 12:4]]. 
2. Ptcp., ὁ μέλλων: absol., [[45-romans.8.38|Rom.8:38]], [[46-1-corinthians.3.22|1Co.3:22]]; τὰ μ., [[51-colossians.2.17|Col.2:17;]] εἰς τὸ μ. (Field, _Notes_, 65); with subst., [[40-matthew.3.7|Mat.3:7 12:32]] (ὁ αἰὼν ὁ μ.; LXX for עַד), [[44-acts.24.25|Act.24:25]], [[54-1-timothy.4.8|1Ti.4:8]], [[58-hebrews.2.5|Heb.2:5]], al. 
(AS)

3307:
**μερίζω**
(μέρος), [in LXX chiefly for חָלַק ;] 
**to divide**; 
(a) **to divide into parts **: metaphorically, pass., [[46-1-corinthians.7.34|1Co.7:34]] (WH, R, ing.), [[46-1-corinthians.7.34|1Co.7:34]] (Rec., R, txt.) ( reading and punctuation, see _ICC_, in l); μεμέρισται ὁ Χριστός, [[46-1-corinthians.1.13|1Co.1:13;]] as in late authors, of factional division (cf. Polyb., viii, 23, 9), καθ᾽ ἑαυτοῦ, [[40-matthew.12.25|Mat.12:25;]] ἐφ᾽ εαυτόν, [[40-matthew.12.26|Mat.12:26]], [[41-mark.3.24|Mrk.3:24-26]]; 
(b) **to distribute**: with accusative of thing(s) and dative of person(s), [[41-mark.6.41|Mrk.6:41;]] as in later usage (cf. Polyb., xi, 28, 9), **to bestow**: [[45-romans.12.3|Rom.12:3]], [[46-1-corinthians.7.17|1Co.7:17]], [[47-2-corinthians.10.13|2Co.10:13]], [[58-hebrews.7.2|Heb.7:2]]; mid., with accusative of thing(s) before μετά, [[42-luke.12.13|Luk.12:13]] (cf. δια-, συμ-μερίζω).
(AS)

3392:
**μιαίνω **
[in LXX chiefly for טָמֵא ;] 
1. to dye or stain. 
2. **to stain, defile, soil**; 
(a) **in physical sense**; 
(b) **in moral sense **: [[56-titus.1.15|Tit.1:15]], [[58-hebrews.12.15|Heb.12:15]], Ju 8; 
(with) in ritual sense (cf. [[03-leviticus.22.5|Lev.22:5]], al.): [[43-john.18.28|Jhn.18:28]].
_SYN._: μολύνω, to besmear, which also differs from μ. in that it is never used, as μ. in its primary meaning, in an honourable sense (cf. Tr., _Syn._, § xxxi) (AS)

3398:
**μικρός**, -ά, -όν 
[in LXX chiefly for קָטָן, מָעַט ;] 
**small, little**; 
1. **of persons**; 
(a) lit., of stature: [[41-mark.15.40|Mrk.15:40]] (MM, iii, xvi; on the view that age is meant, see Deiss., BS, 144), [[42-luke.19.3|Luk.19:3;]] οἱ μ., the little ones, [[40-matthew.18.6|Mat.18:6, 10 18:14]], [[41-mark.9.42|Mrk.9:42]]; 
(b) hence metaphorically, of rank or influence (cf. Dalman, _Words_, 113 f.) : [[40-matthew.10.42|Mat.10:42]], [[42-luke.17.2|Luk.17:2]], [[44-acts.8.10|Act.8:10 26:22]], [[58-hebrews.8.11|Heb.8:11]]" (LXX), [[66-revelation.11.18|Rev.11:18 13:16 19:5, 18 20:12]]; compar., -ότερος, [[40-matthew.11.11|Mat.11:11]], [[42-luke.7.28|Luk.7:28 9:48]]. 
2. **Of things**; 
(a) **of size **: [[40-matthew.13.32|Mat.13:32]] [[41-mark.4.31|Mrk.4:31]], [[59-james.3.5|Jas.3:5]]; 
(b) **of quantity**: [[42-luke.12.32|Luk.12:32]], [[46-1-corinthians.5.6|1Co.5:6]], [[48-galatians.5.9|Gal.5:9]], [[66-revelation.3.8|Rev.3:8]]; 
(with) **of time **: [[43-john.7.33|Jhn.7:33 12:35]], [[66-revelation.6.11|Rev.6:11 20:3]]. 
3. Neut., μικρόν, used adverbially; 
(a) **of distance**: [[40-matthew.26.39|Mat.26:39]], [[41-mark.14.35|Mrk.14:35]]; 
(b) **of quantity**: [[47-2-corinthians.11.1|2Co.11:1 11:16]]; 
(with) **of time **: [[43-john.13.33|Jhn.13:33 14:19 16:16-19]], [[58-hebrews.10.37|Heb.10:37]]; μετὰ μ., [[40-matthew.26.73|Mat.26:73]], [[41-mark.14.70|Mrk.14:70]].
(AS)

