3625:
**οἰκουμένη**, -ης, ἡ
(fern. Pres. pass. ptcp. of οἰκέω; sc. γῆ) [in LXX chiefly for תֵּבֵל, אֶרֶץ ;] 
**the inhabited earth**; 
(a) in cl., the countries occupied by Greeks, as disting. from barbarian lands (Hdt., Dem., al.); 
(b) **in later writers, the Roman world**: [[42-luke.2.1|Luk.2:1]], [[44-acts.11.28|Act.11:28 24:5]]; by meton., of its inhabitants : [[44-acts.17.6|Act.17:6 19:27]]; 
(with) in LXX ([[19-psalms.23.1|Psa.23:1 71:8]], al.) and NT, also of the whole inhabited world: [[40-matthew.24.14|Mat.24:14]], [[42-luke.4.5|Luk.4:5 21:26]], [[45-romans.10.18|Rom.10:18]], [[58-hebrews.1.6|Heb.1:6]], [[66-revelation.3.10|Rev.3:10 16:14]]; by meton. (ut supr.), [[44-acts.17.31|Act.17:31]], [[66-revelation.12.9|Rev.12:9]]; 
(d) of the Messianic age, ἡ οἰ. ἡ μέλλουσα = ὁ αἰὼ ὁ μέλλων: [[58-hebrews.2.5|Heb.2:5.]]
(AS)

