3745:
**ὅσος**, -η, -ον, 
_correlat. of τοσοῦτος, _ 
**how much, how many, how great, how far, how long, as much as**, etc. (= Lat. quantus); 
(a) **of number and quantity**: m. pl., [[40-matthew.14.36|Mat.14:36]], [[41-mark.3.10|Mrk.3:10]], [[45-romans.2.12|Rom.2:12]], al.; n. pl., [[40-matthew.17.12|Mat.17:12]], [[41-mark.10.21|Mrk.10:21]], [[42-luke.11.8|Luk.11:8]], al.; πάτνες (πάντα) ὅ., [[40-matthew.13.46|Mat.13:46]], [[42-luke.4.40|Luk.4:40]], al.; before οὗτοι (ταῦτα), [[45-romans.8.14|Rom.8:14]], [[50-philippians.4.8|Php.4:8]]; with indic., [[41-mark.6.56|Mrk.6:56]], [[66-revelation.3.19|Rev.3:19]]; with subjc. [[41-mark.3.28|Mrk.3:28]], al.; ὅ. ἄν, [[40-matthew.18.18|Mat.18:18]], [[43-john.11.22|Jhn.11:22]], al.; 
(b) **of measure and degree**: [[41-mark.3.8|Mrk.3:8]], [[42-luke.8.39|Luk.8:39]], [[44-acts.9.13|Act.9:13]]; in compar. sent., ὅσον before μᾶλλον, [[41-mark.7.36|Mrk.7:36;]] καθ᾽ ὅσον, with compar.. [[58-hebrews.3.3|Heb.3:3;]] before τοσοῦτο, [[58-hebrews.7.20|Heb.7:20;]] οὕτως, [[58-hebrews.9.27|Heb.9:27;]] τοσαύτῳ, with compar. before ὅσῳ, with compar., [[58-hebrews.1.4|Heb.1:4;]] ἐφ᾽ ὅσον, **inasmuch as**, [[40-matthew.25.40|Mat.25:40, 45]] [[45-romans.11.13|Rom.11:13]]; 
(with) **of space and time**: [[66-revelation.21.16|Rev.21:16;]] ἐφ᾽ ὅσον, **as long as**, [[40-matthew.9.15|Mat.9:15]], [[61-2-peter.1.13|2Pe.1:13]]; ἐφ᾽ ὅ. χρόνον, [[45-romans.7.1|Rom.7:1]], [[46-1-corinthians.7.39|1Co.7:39]], [[48-galatians.4.1|Gal.4:1]]; ἔτι μικρὸν ὅσον ὅσον, **yet how very short a time**, [[58-hebrews.10.37|Heb.10:37]] (LXX). 
(AS)

3748:
**ὅστις**, ἥτις, ὅ τι (also written ὅ, τι and ὅτι; see LS, see word; WH, §411; Tdf., _Pr._, 111), in NT scarcely ever except in nom. (M, _Pr._, 91), the only instance of the oblique cases being found in ἕως ὅτου (see: ἕως), relative of indef. reference (related to simple ὅς as Lat. quisquis to qui), 
**whoever, anyone who**; 
(a) of an indef. person or thing: in general statements, [[40-matthew.5.39|Mat.5:39, 41 13:12]], and freq., [[42-luke.14.27|Luk.14:27]], [[48-galatians.5.4|Gal.5:4]], al.; in relative sentences, [[40-matthew.7.26|Mat.7:26]], [[42-luke.15.7|Luk.15:7]], [[50-philippians.3.7|Php.3:7]], al.; πᾶς, with indic., [[40-matthew.7.24|Mat.7:24 10:32]]; ὅ ἄν (ἐάν), with subjc., [[40-matthew.12.50|Mat.12:50 13:12]], [[43-john.14.13|Jhn.14:13]], [[46-1-corinthians.16.2|1Co.16:2]], [[48-galatians.5.10|Gal.5:10]], al.; 
(b) of a definite person or thing, indicating quality, "either generic,_ which, as other like things,_ or essential, _which by its very nature_" (Hort on [[60-1-peter.2.11|1Pe.2:11]]), **who is such as**: [[40-matthew.2.6|Mat.2:6 7:26]], [[42-luke.2.10|Luk.2:10 7:37]], [[43-john.8.53|Jhn.8:53]], [[44-acts.7.53|Act.7:53]], [[45-romans.6.2|Rom.6:2]], [[46-1-corinthians.3.17|1Co.3:17]], [[48-galatians.4.24|Gal.4:24]], [[49-ephesians.1.23|Eph.1:23]], al.; 
(with) where the relative sentence expresses a reason, consequence, etc. (M, _Pr._, 92), **seeing that he (it, they), and he (it, they)**: [[42-luke.8.3|Luk.8:3 10:42]], [[44-acts.10.47|Act.10:47 11:28]], [[50-philippians.4.3|Php.4:3]], al.; 
(d) as in Ionic and late Greek (Bl., §50, 1; M, _Pr._, l.with), differing but little from ὅς: [[42-luke.2.4|Luk.2:4 9:30]], [[44-acts.17.10|Act.17:10]], [[66-revelation.12.13|Rev.12:13]]. 
(AS)

